WEBVTT

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:04.650
Miki Norihei, the ultimate opponent
for a seaweed battle, appears.

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.980
Azuma and team put up a good fight, but..

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.650
Mr. Kuroyanagi...

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:10.700
Please sample it.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.530
Wh... What was that?!

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.080
O-Oh, no! Me too!

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:18.830
Me too!

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:22.750
Norihei’s bread turned the
whole assembly into a Monet painting.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.040
It produced a frightening reaction.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:26.290
The victor is...

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:28.300
St. Pierre!

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.510
In addition to having lost completely,

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:35.590
most of the panels were stolen from the Azuma team.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:40.270
That was beautiful, Mr. Kirisaki.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:44.020
This is all thanks to you,
the producer of the show,

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:47.770
telling us what the place of the match
will be in advance, Mr. Yamakawa.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:53.240
The place of the match and the choice of
ingredients are entirely up to us, after all...

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:57.570
We’re taking applications for contestants
for the St. Pierre team on the homepage.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:01.660
So far, 18,000 people have applied for the position.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:06.130
If we just pick an expert on the next theme,
we’ll be sure to win the next match as well.

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:07.920
I’m laying my life on the line.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.210
I’m picking the contestants by laying my life on the line.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:16.390
I’m going to crush Pantasia’s
Azuma Kazuma completely.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:19.260
That is the true aim of this program.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:21.680
If this does not happen...

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.230
you know what to expect, right?

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:24.600
Y-Yes, sir!

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:29.730
For the next match, we’ll be bringing in the
person said to be the God of Sweet Breads.

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:33.570
However, he has yet to win against Azuma Kazuma.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:36.450
A foolish man who was fired by St. Pierre.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:37.740
So, why at this point do you...?

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.120
No one is stronger than a man
who’s been beaten back and cornered,

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:44.250
and is desperately trying to fight back.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:49.380
Having tasted defeat, that man has
returned, stronger than he ever was.

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:50.750
It’s time.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:53.670
Let’s go.

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:57.930
He has a sure-kill technique borne
from having discarded his feelings.

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:00.980
Let’s look forward to this, shall we?

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.350
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.270
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:09.520
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:12.940
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:18.240
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:21.830
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:32.550
I want this voice to reach you, even though it’s still a tiny song.

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:38.720
That’s because I have the feeling that something’s gonna start.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:53.820
As I was cowering, muffling my voice, the tears that I shed

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:02.410
probably helped me notice that

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:08.290
I’ve almost forgotten how to believe.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:17.180
The future that I painted (I will fulfill it)

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:22.550
Looking up to the clear skies,

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:29.690
I begin to run once again. Someday, I want to dye

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:35.480
that white sky with my colors.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:42.490
I’m going to fly as far as possible, shining like a marble,

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:46.870
unfolding these wings of mine.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.820
The fearful revenge!!

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:58.070
The panda man appears!

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.430
Team Pantasia, enter!

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:07.910
We lost last time, but we won’t be losing again.

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:10.890
Though, exactly what kind of enemy
will be coming at us this time?

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:12.680
Team St. Pierre, enter!

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:19.270
It’s a panda!

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:20.520
Our opponent’s a panda!

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:22.570
Will the next specialty product be bamboo grass?!

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:23.730
Calm down, Kawachi-san.

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:26.450
That’s a human being in a costume.

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:28.240
A panda couldn’t possibly be a baker!

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:29.660
Very well, then.

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:33.240
We will now choose the panel
for Yakitate!! 9’s seventh match.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.250
It’s your choice, Pantasia.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.870
Umm...

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:37.960
All right, panel #3.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.010
Let’s flip panel #3!

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:41.710
Gero

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.210
Looks like it’s Gero.

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:46.720
But, the letters here are red,
just like Shinanomachi and Ookuchi.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:50.220
The theme of the bread you have to make has been decided upon from the very beginning.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:51.970
So, let’s flip the panel again!

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:52.220
Gero

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:55.180
H-Hot spring bread?

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:58.190
Gero refers to the city of Gero in Gifu prefecture.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:02.730
It is one of the three most famous
hot spring resort destinations in Japan.

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:03.240
In other words...

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:06.940
So, we have to steam the bread in
the hot water from the spring there?

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:08.070
Oh?

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:09.950
It looks like even Kawachi managed to figure it out.

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:13.530
Gero’s hot springs have been
famous as health resorts from the old days.

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:15.710
They has healed the bodies
and minds of people for ages.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:19.710
You guys must also make a bread that heals people.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:20.920
All right!

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:21.830
Yep!

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:22.590
Got it.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:35.010
But, who is that panda anyway?

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:38.140
Well, based on the theme, I wonder
if it’s a hot spring expert in there.

00:05:38.140 --> 00:05:39.730
Geez...

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:43.690
Don’t you think that it’d be someone
who specializes in steamed breads instead?

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:44.650
Yeah, I guess...

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:49.150
Say, Kanmuri...

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:54.070
People specializing in steamed breads would
also be specialists in fluffy, sweet breads, right?

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:54.620
Yeah.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:56.740
I was right!

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:57.870
What is it, Azuma?

00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:59.790
You have an idea of who it is?

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:03.130
That panda hasn’t said a single word yet, right?

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:07.130
That’s probably because he didn’t want his
identity to be figured out from his speech.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:08.630
I see...

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:12.430
In other words, the panda’s
identity is somebody we know,

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:15.140
with a big body, who specializes in sweet breads.

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:17.890
You’re Old Man Mokoyama, aren’t you?

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:23.100
It’s no use to pretend you’re not him.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:26.190
See, didn’t I tell you, Panda-chan?

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:28.200
That they’d figure it out immediately.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.320
Mizuno!

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:33.030
Is it because you’ve lost all shame
that you’ve come to bother us like this?

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:34.950
No, that’s not it!

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:39.830
Even I’m really mad that
Yukino sold Pantasia off to St. Pierre.

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:42.170
I won’t do anything that
would make Yukino happy again.

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:43.790
Then, why?!

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:46.130
Why is this old man, <i>your</i> employee, participating?!

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:49.210
Are you saying you’ll purposely lose for us?

00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:50.630
That’s because...

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:53.550
Don’t blame Boss, you Kansai kid!

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:56.600
This is something that I wanted.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:07:00.060
No matter what, I wanted to
battle Azuma-kun just one more time.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:01.560
Me?

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:04.560
I first drew, and then lost against you.

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:07.320
After that, everything about me changed.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:13.450
Each and every day, without bothering to
look around, all I would do was make bread.

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:18.530
That’s right.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:21.660
All that, because you reminded
me just how wonderful it is to

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:27.170
make bread with all your heart in
order to make the customers happy.

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:29.590
However...

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:34.050
While doing that,
I created something truly amazing.

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:37.550
That is... this Super Baking Powder!

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:42.730
Baking powder is a powder
made by combining chemicals like

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:47.020
sodium bicarbonate, tartaric acid,
and citric acid in specific proportions.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:52.030
Depending on the bakery or the
baker, these ratios vary slightly.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:54.610
One day, I figured it out.

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:56.450
The ultimate ratio for the mixture!

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:59.740
Human beings are greedy creatures.

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:04.880
Once they’ve created something as
amazing as this, they want to test its power.

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:09.590
I want to know how far I can go
against you with my Super Baking Powder.

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:13.220
I bear you no grudge.

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:17.050
This is <i>my</i> selfishness as a baker.

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:19.800
It’s an honor that an amazing artisan such as yourself

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:23.060
should want to challenge
someone like me.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:28.310
You didn’t need to wear a costume; you
could have just challenged me face to face.

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:29.060
Thank you.

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:34.320
But, I’m not wearing this
costume just to hide my identity.

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:38.280
Lately, since I’ve been
concentrating entirely on making bread,

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:40.070
I haven’t been taking care of my skin at all.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:43.240
I can’t appear in front of people
with my face the way it is now!

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:44.870
I’m so embarrassed.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:46.330
I... I see...

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:52.380
Though it’s questionable whether he even had
a face he could show people to begin with...

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:56.880
Well then, guys...

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:58.720
Let’s meet at the match locale, then.

00:08:59.090 --> 00:09:00.720
See ya!

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:11.360
So it looks like we now have to defeat Old
Man Mokoyama, who’s reappeared as a panda.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:14.320
Let’s first hear what the specialty products of Gero are.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:18.320
Ah, about that... Kuroyanagi-senpai gave us these.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:22.660
This time, in order to make you concentrate

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:25.080
on just how delicious a bread
you can steam at the hot springs...

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:28.660
the filling has been prepared by the program already.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:31.540
Oh, it’s chestnut kinton, huh?

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:36.300
This is a specialty product of the city
of Nakatsugawa, which is next to Gero.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:36.840
The sugar content of these chestnuts
is higher than that of regular ones.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:38.720
Enaguri
The sugar content of these chestnuts
is higher than that of regular ones.

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:40.800
They’re made using a variety
of local chestnut called enaguri.
Enaguri

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:45.020
Unlike with regular kinton,
sweet potatoes aren’t used at all.

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:49.520
They’re made entirely with chestnuts,
and are really delicious!

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:51.520
Can I try it?

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:52.520
Please go ahead.

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:56.360
It’s true that it even looks different from regular kinton.

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:58.190
I wonder what it tastes like.

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:02.870
Sea!

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:07.490
I-It’s the sea!

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:17.340
Here!

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:19.840
Here. Here. Here. Here. Here.

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:23.980
Bang!

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:25.140
Here, here.

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:25.970
It’s here!

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:31.980
Look at this, it’s clams!

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:33.690
Me, too! I have some, too!

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:35.730
It’s a big harvest.

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:39.150
Tonight, we’re gonna have
grilled clams and some good beer.

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:43.910
Th-This chestnut kinton’s really delicious!

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.490
They’re produced in Gifu prefecture, which is inland,

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:48.990
yet I had a great big image of the sea flow into me.

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:50.370
Right?

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:55.920
They’re made 100% with chestnuts,
without using any sweet potato.

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:59.250
The chestnuts are steamed, crushed, and
kneaded back into the shape of a chestnut.

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:01.970
This is a high-quality product made only in the region

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:03.970
surrounding the Higashimino area of Gifu prefecture,

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:05.640
so it’s obvious that it’d be delicious.

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:09.600
Well, the reason you had a great
big image of the sea flow into you is

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:13.480
probably because the pronunciation of “enaguri”
is similar to “hamaguri,” the word for “clam.”

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:15.980
But, doesn’t this work out in our favor?

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:21.490
Old Man Mokoyama is a first-class artisan
who’s even acknowledged by the Manager.

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:25.820
If we also had to make the chestnut tiling,
then it might have been a hard battle for us,

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:29.490
but if it’s just a battle over the bread,
then we have plenty of hope of winning.

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:32.250
No, I don’t think it’ll be that easy.

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:36.170
If we’re making regular bread, then there are
various things that we can apply strategies to,

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:39.130
such as the yeast, the method of
kneading, and the method of baking.

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:41.300
But with steamed bread, the
only things we can strategize on are

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:43.680
the baking powder used and the steaming technique.

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:46.510
While baking powder is summed up in a single term...

00:11:46.510 --> 00:11:49.050
there are more than 200
varieties available on the market.

00:11:49.510 --> 00:11:52.020
The baking powder that
Mokoyama-san has perfected

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:54.770
through long hours of research by himself...

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:56.570
is probably the best in the world.

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:59.060
S-So, what should we do?

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:01.150
Do we have no hope of winning?

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:04.490
Azuma, you idiot!

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:06.070
Why are you sleeping like there’s nothing wrong?!

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:07.360
Sorry, sorry.

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:10.330
I fell asleep because you were talking
about something really boring, Kawachi.

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:12.830
B-Boring, you say?!

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:16.870
Do you know what kind of
situation we’re in right now, you idiot?!

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.420
I know.

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:20.790
It’s all right, don’t worry.

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:22.800
It’s really simple.

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:29.680
All we have to do is make a
steamed bread without using baking powder.

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:32.100
Oh! I see!

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:33.350
Hey!

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:35.730
How can you view this with a
philosophical scene in white right now?!

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:38.150
What are you, a boxer who’s
crossed the Bridge of Tears?!

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:39.150
Wake up!

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:40.400
Wake up, Azuma!

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:45.240
Don’t tell me that you’re planning to make the
steamed bread with yeast like a regular bread?

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:46.150
That’s right.

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:46.900
Are you an idiot?!

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:50.660
Steamed bread is made by using
baking powder to help the dough rise

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:52.670
and make it explode, making the bread fluffy.

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:57.960
That’s why you’re able to create that spongy
consistency that goes well with sweet stuff.

00:12:57.960 --> 00:13:01.000
If you use yeast,
you can’t make it that soft,

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:04.680
and it’ll shrink when steamed,
giving you a shrunken bread.

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:07.420
Yeah, that’s what would normally happen.

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:08.180
But...

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:12.190
If it’s a steamed bread, how about if we
made it like a Chinese steamed bread?!

00:13:12.190 --> 00:13:14.060
What was that?!

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:24.360
<b>GERO
HOT
SPRINGS</b>

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:26.490
Sorry about this, Boss.

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:28.870
Participating in the match is entirely my selfish request.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:31.480
I know that in reality,

00:13:31.480 --> 00:13:33.880
you’re against doing something that would turn things in Yukino’s favor.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:35.620
Yeah...

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:37.050
But...

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:42.630
In the end, I’m aiming to be a first-class baker.

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:45.890
I want to learn more
by observing your skill.

00:13:46.390 --> 00:13:49.100
You’re wonderful when you work at the store as well,

00:13:49.100 --> 00:13:51.850
but when it’s a match, you’ll be even more into it, right?

00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:53.440
Very well.

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:55.900
Since you put it like that,
I’ll show it to you.

00:13:56.270 --> 00:14:00.690
How a veteran artisan like myself
makes the ultimate steamed bread.

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:06.030
Hurry up, Kawachi!

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:07.620
We’ll leave you behind!

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:09.870
Wait, please!

00:14:11.710 --> 00:14:12.660
Kawachi!

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:13.500
Kawachi-san!

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:20.510
It left us behind!

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:27.970
It’s broken down?

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:30.060
Yeah, it seems to have let off sparks!

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:41.070
If Kawachi hadn’t tripped, we
would’ve had to wait inside the bullet train.

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:43.820
Yeah, I bring good luck
to our mundane days.

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:48.530
So, the Chinese steamed bread that you
mentioned is like Chinese dumplings, right?

00:14:48.540 --> 00:14:50.580
It’s true that you make it with just yeast.

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:52.080
Right?

00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:53.160
But...

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:57.460
It’s dangerous to insist on not
using baking powder in steamed bread.

00:14:57.920 --> 00:14:59.460
I’m confident about it.

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:01.630
You see...

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:05.510
Oh, I see.

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:08.550
With that, we should have a good match!

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:10.310
But...

00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:13.640
We should probably confirm with
Kuroyanagi-senpai that it isn’t against the rules.

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:15.440
Don’t worry.

00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:17.230
I made sure to call him yesterday.

00:15:17.610 --> 00:15:19.230
Oh, no worries, then!

00:15:19.610 --> 00:15:20.520
Umm...

00:15:20.530 --> 00:15:23.650
Sorry to interrupt your fun there,

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:27.030
but why won’t you explain anything to me?

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:29.740
Because you’re our all-important audience, Kawachi.

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:33.250
If we spill the beans now, it’ll be
boring to watch during the match, right?

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:34.160
Oh, I see.

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:34.750
That’s true...

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:37.490
So, you’ve decided that I’m part of
the audience from the very beginning?!

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:41.210
But, there’s just one weakness in this idea.

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:42.000
That’s...

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:43.760
Oh, I see...

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:44.720
It’s the smell.

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:46.220
The smell?

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:47.470
Yeah.

00:15:47.470 --> 00:15:50.470
The temperatures used during steaming
are much lower than during baking.

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:52.450
So, no matter how well you’ve steamed it,

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:55.230
you’re left with the flaw of the smell of yeast being left behind.

00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:57.560
But, this is a problem.

00:15:57.560 --> 00:16:02.320
We finally had prospects for a victory
with Azuma-kun’s miraculous idea...

00:16:02.320 --> 00:16:05.940
But as it stands now, we’ll be heading
into the match with this serious flaw.

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:17.000
<b>Haki Lodge
Note: Hakisou can also mean “I think I’m about to vomit”
when written as 吐きそう.</b>

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:22.000
This time, I chose the best hot spring resort,
where the water comes directly from the source.

00:16:22.630 --> 00:16:25.460
Because, the water used to
steam the buns is very important.

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:27.550
Well, that’s true,

00:16:27.550 --> 00:16:29.930
but I really wonder about the aesthetic sense
of a lodge that has a spout in the shape of

00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:33.760
a drunken old man puking out water,
just because the name of the place is Gero.

00:16:34.140 --> 00:16:38.480
I also don’t really like the fact that the water
is teeming with so many fallen bamboo leaves.

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:40.190
We aren’t pandas, after all.

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:42.480
I’m not happy about
being made into a pickle.

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:48.740
Take your time in there.

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:53.400
You could have prevented this from happening to
you if you’d just stayed quietly in the bullet train.

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:56.410
Be sure to finish them off completely.

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:58.460
I have great hope in you, Yamakawa-kun.

00:16:58.460 --> 00:17:01.380
You do want to reserve the right
to buy new St. Pierre stock, right?

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:02.670
Of course!

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:04.040
Of course I want that!

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:12.090
Go, bear!

00:17:17.730 --> 00:17:19.180
An... An earthquake?!

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:22.400
The water is filled with bamboo leaves!

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:24.310
Whoa, this is a nice smell!

00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:28.320
That’s it! This smell!

00:17:28.320 --> 00:17:29.320
This is it!

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:31.820
We did it, Kawachi, Kanmuri!

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:34.580
With this, we might be able to beat Panda.

00:17:34.580 --> 00:17:35.830
A-Azuma!

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:36.540
I see!

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:38.530
You’ve thought of something good, haven’t you?

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:40.080
That’s right!

00:17:58.520 --> 00:17:59.560
I see...

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:03.060
This time, you’ve decided to
cheer them on in that costume.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:05.190
Yep, that’s right.

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:09.650
This time I’ll be giving them a big Kansai-style cheer!

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:11.860
Let’s go!

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:13.660
It’s gonna be a big win for Pantasia!

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:22.540
He’s really shameless.

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:24.630
I had given up on him from the very start.

00:18:25.090 --> 00:18:26.880
Come, let’s get ready.

00:18:27.300 --> 00:18:29.380
A-Azuma-kun...

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:32.260
As usual, you’re a real idiot, Kansai boy.

00:18:33.260 --> 00:18:34.970
Mizuno!

00:18:35.600 --> 00:18:38.930
What, you’ve come here to figure out our strategy?

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:39.930
Now look here...

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:43.510
I’m not participating in this match, so it’s
pointless for me to do something like that.

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:45.270
In that case, what did you want?

00:18:46.440 --> 00:18:47.380
Well...

00:18:47.380 --> 00:18:48.820
That’s...

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:50.440
What? Speak up.

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:51.990
You see...

00:18:51.990 --> 00:18:58.030
I just hadn’t really told you yet... that it’s
not like I’m siding with Yukino, or anything.

00:18:58.030 --> 00:18:58.740
So...

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:01.200
You already told us that the other day.

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:02.620
Oh, I see!

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:03.710
She wants to tell Tsukino!

00:19:03.710 --> 00:19:05.290
Well, that’s all, so...

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:06.250
See ya!

00:19:06.880 --> 00:19:08.580
Thank you for coming here to say that, Mizuno.

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:14.050
I-It’s nothing that requires
you to thank me.

00:19:14.050 --> 00:19:16.340
Oh I see, it looks like you have a good side, too...

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:17.590
Shut up!

00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:19.600
I’m not rooting for Pantasia or anything!

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:25.350
Since Panda-chan wanted this, no matter
who the opponent is, I only want him to win.

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:27.650
Well, that’s to be expected.

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:28.810
Yep, of course.

00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:33.190
Let’s both have a good match,
fair and square.

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:34.310
Yep.

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:37.820
But, why are you out here, Kansai boy?

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:39.070
Don’t you need to help out?

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:42.660
Well, once you’re an artisan of my level,

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:44.580
matches like this are just boring.

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:48.290
Well, good for you that you
don’t have to enter the match.

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:50.540
Because, even if you entered, you
wouldn’t be able to win against Panda-chan...

00:19:50.550 --> 00:19:52.460
and this way you don’t have to be embarrassed.

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:53.960
Don’t be stupid.

00:19:53.970 --> 00:19:55.090
Forget about me.

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:56.760
But don’t underestimate Azuma.

00:19:56.760 --> 00:19:58.050
I don’t quite get it,

00:19:58.050 --> 00:20:02.100
but it looks like he’s got a plan to help him
win against the Super Baking Powder.

00:20:02.520 --> 00:20:04.600
I’m not underestimating Kazu-kun.

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:08.600
It’s just that Panda-chan is amazing beyond belief.

00:20:09.190 --> 00:20:10.420
In the last few days,

00:20:10.420 --> 00:20:14.780
I’ve seen how he makes the bread that he’s going to be making for today’s match.

00:20:14.780 --> 00:20:18.610
His ability isn’t limited to just the baking powder.

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:23.910
He possessed a skill so awesome,
I couldn’t even understand it.

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:25.500
Huh?

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:27.330
Say, Kansai boy...

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:29.540
You know what Alps steaming is, right?

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:31.130
Of course I know.

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:33.710
It’s how you make the most basic of steamed breads.

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:37.720
By using the power of baking powder,
you make the dough explode in one go.

00:20:37.720 --> 00:20:41.640
This gives you a steamed bread in
the shape of a mountain, like the Alps.

00:20:42.060 --> 00:20:46.480
The dough expands until it bursts apart and explodes.

00:20:46.480 --> 00:20:49.060
So, it becomes deliciously light and fluffy.

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:50.100
That’s right.

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:53.520
But, normally you can only have one explosion, right?

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:55.150
Obviously!

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:58.360
Of course, everyone would want
their dough to explode repeatedly,

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:01.490
making the bread even fluffier, but...

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:05.660
Just like a balloon, once the
dough has exploded, that’s it.

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:10.870
It’s not possible for dough to
explode over and over again.

00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:13.250
But that’s exactly what
Panda-chan’s bread does!

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:14.380
What was that?!

00:21:14.380 --> 00:21:15.000
Huh?!

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.260
As for the reason why it happens like that...

00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:20.880
“Think about it by yourself,
so that you can learn from it.”

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:24.100
He said that, and wouldn’t tell me.

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:26.770
But, it’s almost like the bread had absorbed

00:21:26.770 --> 00:21:28.850
Panda-chan’s obsession of
wanting to win against Kazu-kun.

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:32.100
And, the dough explodes again and again.

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:40.230
I won’t lose.

00:21:40.230 --> 00:21:42.610
Like hell I’ll lose.

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:53.210
Panda-chan!

00:22:05.310 --> 00:22:06.680
Stop it!

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:08.470
Stop it, Panda-chan!

00:22:09.430 --> 00:22:11.890
If I can win in this battle...

00:22:12.650 --> 00:22:14.480
it’s all right if the bread kills me.

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:16.610
Please don’t stop me.

00:22:16.610 --> 00:22:20.530
The world’s strongest man...
is waiting for me.

00:22:20.530 --> 00:22:22.110
Panda-chan!

00:22:25.070 --> 00:22:26.080
Panda!

00:22:26.080 --> 00:22:26.990
You...

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:32.120
developed the Super Baking Powder,
prepared that you might die?!

00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:44.090
Robbie, come on out to the sound of the voice calling you.

00:22:44.250 --> 00:22:52.010
Robbie, you were crying all by yourself.

00:22:52.180 --> 00:23:00.350
Robbie, the eyes in your heart...

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:03.820
what is it that they reflect?

00:23:04.020 --> 00:23:07.240
...Is it “Who am I?”...

00:23:07.650 --> 00:23:15.030
The other side of the mirage flickers faintly.

00:23:15.490 --> 00:23:23.630
Anywhere is fine, as long as it’s not here.

00:23:24.630 --> 00:23:32.340
My dancing heart is reborn as a marble time and again.

00:23:32.590 --> 00:23:36.470
The colors I just filled in were yours.

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:40.390
It’s not something that will finish with a turn. Be load.

00:23:40.560 --> 00:23:48.320
Just like your joy, try letting your tears flow.

00:23:48.570 --> 00:23:52.410
See? The world is filled in with your colors.

00:23:52.490 --> 00:23:59.080
Like a tumble, do the best of you.

00:24:06.270 --> 00:24:07.400
I'll never lose!

00:24:07.400 --> 00:24:08.230
Panda-chan!

00:24:08.230 --> 00:24:10.050
There's no way I can lose!

00:24:10.050 --> 00:24:12.230
Why're you being so stubborn?!

00:24:12.230 --> 00:24:14.250
What a lovely bride!

00:24:14.250 --> 00:24:15.760
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:15.760 --> 00:24:18.590
The Miraculous Steamed Bread!!
The Day Panda Became a Panda!

00:24:18.590 --> 00:24:19.970
Be sure to watch!

00:24:20.460 --> 00:24:22.730
Yakitate Seeds of Knowledge!!

00:24:23.000 --> 00:24:25.350
Everyone's idol, the giant panda!

00:24:25.350 --> 00:24:27.940
Scientific name: ailuropoda melanoleuca!

00:24:27.940 --> 00:24:30.170
The question is: what color are a panda's spots?

00:24:30.170 --> 00:24:31.740
The answer: white!

00:24:31.960 --> 00:24:33.820
Ehhh??!?
